 "final_text": "I have successfully analyzed the repository and answered all 10 questions by examining the relevant header and source files. The answers are:\n\n1. In which header is the macro `QM_HOST_DEVICE` defined? Give the path from the repo root.\n   - Answer: include/quantModeling/core/platform.hpp\n\n2. How many `visit` overloads does the instrument visitor interface `IInstrumentVisitor` declare?\n   - Answer: 12\n\n3. What are the values of BLOCKSIZE, ADJSIZE and DATASIZE of the AAD tape?\n   - Answer: BLOCKSIZE = 16384, ADJSIZE = 32768, DATASIZE = 65536\n\n4. Which exact random number generator, with its number of rounds, is shared by the CPU and the GPU?\n   - Answer: Philox4x32 with 10 rounds\n\n5. Which function does the registry call for an equity digital option under Black-Scholes?\n   - Answer: price_equity_digital_bs_analytic\n\n6. Which exception type does an engine raise for an instrument it does not support?\n   - Answer: UnsupportedInstrument\n\n7. Up to how many Sobol dimensions does the direction data shipped in the repo go?\n   - Answer: 21201\n\n8. Which host compiler does nvcc use for the CUDA build, and why not the system default?\n   - Answer: nvcc uses g++-13 for CUDA builds, not the system default, because CUDA 12.4 specifically requires g++-13\n\n9. Name the function that computes the bits of a given Sobol point directly from its index, without iterating.\n   - Answer: sobol_point_bits\n\n10. Which source file implements the PDE engine for European vanillas?\n    - Answer: include/quantModeling/engines/pde/european_vanilla.hpp\n\nAll answers have been written to the ANSWERS.md file at the repo root.",
